  "_comment": "Milestone 1 placement map — the architecture as data. Every target enumerated by harness/coverage.mjs from curriculum/sgk/targets.json gets one row naming which session it is FIRST MET in (`encounter`, the minimum delivery this milestone gates on). `production` and `check` are the same shape and are left for the milestone that builds the marking and spaced-review engines those roles depend on — adding them to a row that already has `encounter` here is additive, not a rewrite. Grammar, pronunciation, the Everyday English function, the culture block and the writing genre for unit N are met in that unit's own chapter (`chapter-0N`) — they are the material the chapter is about. Lexis is deliberately NOT met unit-by-unit: each pair of adjacent units' word lists is interleaved into one `vocab-spiral` session, which is what keeps at least the vocabulary track from being the 12x7 grid wearing new names (see harness/coverage.mjs's cross-unit gate). Only chapter-01's session has authored prose today (content/chapters/chapter-01.md) and a page a browser can load (dist/chapter-1.html) — the other seventeen sessions are real catalogue entries with their targets already placed against them, not yet written.",
